983	     * {@link #rejectDuplicateIdentity}) yet whose {@code soundex(lastName)} and postcode both match an
984	     * existing owner's. Because the telephone is part of the identity key, two owners that share a last
985	     * name and postcode but carry different telephones have different identity keys, so the second is
986	     * created as a soft match rather than rejected. When such a match exists the owner is created with
987	     * {@code possibleDuplicate} set to {@code true} and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} set to the matching
988	     * owner's id (the earliest matching owner by id); otherwise {@code possibleDuplicate} is
989	     * {@code false} and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} is left unset.
990	     *
991	     * <p>An owner that declares household membership via {@code sharesHousehold} is never flagged: a
992	     * declared household member is not a suspected duplicate. An owner without a postcode cannot match
993	     * on postcode and so is never flagged.
994	     *
995	     * @param owner           the owner being created, with its telephone, email, postcode and last
996	     *                        name already set
997	     * @param sharesHousehold whether the owner declared itself a member of an existing household
998	     */
999	    private void applyPossibleDuplicate(Owner owner, boolean sharesHousehold) {
1000	        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(false);
1001	        if (sharesHousehold) {
1002	            return;
1003	        }
1004	        String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
1005	        if (postcode == null) {
1006	            return;
1007	        }
1008	        String soundex = owner.getLastNameSoundex();
1009	        String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
1010	        Owner match = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
1011	            .filter(this::isNotDeleted)
1012	            .filter(existing -> !identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey())
1013	                && soundex.equals(existing.getLastNameSoundex())
1014	                && postcode.equals(existing.getPostcode()))
1015	            .min(Comparator.comparingInt(Owner::getId))
1016	            .orElse(null);
1017	        if (match != null) {
1018	            owner.setPossibleDuplicate(true);
1019	            owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(match.getId());
1020	        }
1021	    }
